# Fault F7 (W-A): a name in a def key bind's `where` was never checked, so reading the def failed inside the
# interpreter (`AttributeError '_r'`). L §2.3 `bind`: a key bind may carry `where`; L §5.6: the def is defined where
# its key bind's where holds. blue is not red and not warm, so v[blue] = 1 in both texts (q, q2); and warm, read by
# v's key bind, is read (no WARN-UNREAD).
=== m.tally
model t7
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2021-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index colour = [red, blue, green]
def warm[c in colour]: bool = c == red
def v[c in colour where not warm[c]]: int = 1
def w[c in colour where c != red]: int = 1

ask q: v[blue]
ask q2: w[blue]
=== expect
q: 1
  cut 2026-01-15
q2: 1
  cut 2026-01-15
